-*   `chunk`: Max rays per forward pass to limit VRAM (e.g., 4096) [S5, S7, unofficial].
+*   $N_{rand}$ (Batch Size): 1024 or 2048 rays per iteration [S5, S11, unofficial].
+*   Learning Rate ($\eta$): $5 \times 10^{-4}$ for Adam [S11, unofficial].
+*   Decay Rate: 0.1 [S6, S18, unofficial].
+*   Decay Steps: $1000 \times \text{args.lrate\_decay}$ (e.g., 100,000 steps if decay starts after 100k) [S5, S18, unofficial].
+*   Total Iterations ($N_{iters}$): 100,000 to 1,000,000 [S11, S14, unofficial].
+*   Chunk Size: Max rays processed per forward pass to limit VRAM (e.g., 8192) [S5, unofficial].
 
 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **VRAM Overflow:** Rendering all rays at once can exceed GPU memory. Mitigated by chunking rays [S5, S7, unofficial].
-*   **Gradient Graph Freeing:** Higher-order derivatives (e.g., for logging gradients) must be computed before `loss.backward()` [S3, unofficial].
-*   **Checkpoint Resumption:** When resuming, the scheduler's last epoch must be set to `start_epoch - 1` to maintain correct decay [S9, unofficial].
-*   **Instability in Growth:** In dynamic growth methods, randomly initialized sub-networks may collapse to zero density. Initialize grown sub-network alpha weights to match the parent [S1].
+*   **VRAM Overflow:** Rendering all rays at once can exceed GPU memory. Mitigated by chunking rays into smaller batches during the forward pass [S5, unofficial].
+*   **Empty Checkpoints:** Loading a checkpoint with step 0 is considered an error/empty state [S15, unofficial].
+*   **Scheduler Resumption:** When resuming, the scheduler's last epoch must be set to `start_epoch - 1` to maintain correct decay [S9, unofficial].
+*   **Instability in Growing Networks:** Directly initializing grown sub-networks randomly causes instability; weights should be inherited from the parent network [S1].
 
